Template: inputloop-gitcha-runner/server_url
Type: string
Default:
Description: Gitcha server this runner takes jobs from (empty: register by hand later):
 The server's public URL, for example https://gitcha.example.org.  With a
 registration token below, the runner registers itself during installation.

Template: inputloop-gitcha-runner/registration_token
Type: password
Description: Registration token from that server:
 An administrator makes one for instance-wide runners, a team owner for a
 team's.  A token made with "uses" greater than one can register a whole
 fleet.  It is used once, here, and not kept: the runner keeps the runner token
 it is given instead, in /var/lib/gitcha-runner/runner.json (mode 600).

Template: inputloop-gitcha-runner/name
Type: string
Default:
Description: Name for this runner (empty: the host name):

Template: inputloop-gitcha-runner/labels
Type: string
Default:
Description: Extra labels for this runner (comma list, may be empty):
 Pipelines and functions can ask for runners by label.

Template: inputloop-gitcha-runner/enable
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Enable and start the gitcha-runner service now?
 It needs a registered runner and bContain.  If not now, later:
 systemctl enable --now gitcha-runner
